@9 = ~We found this rare material. Can you make something out of it? It's from a manticore.~
@10 = ~Have you finished the armor made from the manticore hide?~
@11 = ~Helm almighty, a manticore? I... I won't even ask where you obtained such a wonderful craft, as I'm sure you didn't actually beat a manticore. It borders on impossible. This material is perfect for exceptionally durable hide armor. I could make such armor for you, but I require 5,000 gold coins and three days to work it. If you're interested. You can also sell it to me for the same price, and I shall put it into stock for some merchants.~
@12 = ~Interested. Here's 5,000 gold coins.~
@13 = ~No. I think I'll sell it instead.~
@14 = ~Aye. Finished it. The hide was unlike anything I've worked with before - tough as old oak, but it took the needle cleanly once I found the grain. Here. Manticore's Mane. Treat it well.~
